.TH CCOL_SELECTABLE_FROM_DYNQ 3 "2026-07-12" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
ccol_selectable_from_dynq \- build a ccol_selectable from a ccol_dynamic_queue
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_selectable_from_dynq(q, dir);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Builds a ccol_selectable value (a tagged union, here of type
ccol_selectable_dynq) that wraps the given ccol_dynamic_queue pointer
with the given direction.

  ccol_select_read; wait for at least one message to arrive (read-wait)
  ccol_select_write; wait until the queue holds fewer than
                     ccol_max_elem_count messages, the same ceiling
                     ccol_dynmq_send_zc() itself enforces, or until
                     sends on the queue are turned off

In practice a ccol_dynamic_queue has no bound, so the write direction
is nearly always ready at once. A queue whose sends were turned off
with ccol_dynmq_disable_sending() is ready too, the same way a pipe
whose reader has gone is ready for POLLOUT, and the
ccol_dynmq_send_zc() that the caller makes next returns
ccol_not_permitted.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
q    ccol_dynamic_queue pointer to wrap. A NULL value makes a
     selectable that ccol_select() rejects with ccol_invalid_args.
dir  ccol_select_read or ccol_select_write.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_selectable value (not a pointer).
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ccol_dynamic_queue *dq = ccol_dynamic_queue_create(NULL);
ccol_circular_queue *q0 = ccol_circular_queue_create(8, NULL);

size_t idx;
ccol_select_va(&idx,
    ccol_selectable_from_circq(q0, ccol_select_read),
    ccol_selectable_from_dynq(dq, ccol_select_read));
/* on ccol_success, claim the message with ccol_dynmq_try_recv_zc(dq, ...)
   or ccol_circq_try_recv_zc(q0, ...), for whichever selectable idx
   points at */

ccol_dynamic_queue_destroy(dq);
ccol_circular_queue_destroy(q0);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_select (3),
.BR ccol_select_va (3),
.BR ccol_selectable_from_circq (3),
.BR ccol_selectable_from_chan (3),
.BR ccol_selectable_from_fd (3)
